DomainSuffix.description:
Canonical DNS suffix. A bare domain matches itself and descendant labels;
a leading `*.` is accepted only as an explicit spelling of that same
complete-label boundary rule. It never performs substring matching.

relay_governance.description:
Owner-visible, bounded Relay governance observations. This remains
absent for older snapshots, disabled Relays and non-owner projections;
adapters must not infer an empty ledger from a missing field.

traffic_session.description:
Runtime-authoritative local traffic-protection session. `Protected` is
emitted only after fresh TUN, route, DNS and reachability validation;
migration and failure states are never inferred by UI adapters.
